export const html = "<p>These Terms are an agreement between you and <strong>Availeron Consulting, Inc.</strong>, a New York corporation, 745 5th Ave., Suite 500, New York, NY 10151, United States (\"we\", \"us\"), which operates Overhype.me (the \"Service\"). By creating an account or using the Service you agree to these Terms, to our <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>, our <a href=\"/copyright\">Copyright Policy</a> and our <a href=\"/guidelines\">Community Guidelines</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.</p>\n<h2>1. Who may use Overhype.me</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You must be 18 or older.</strong> Overhype.me is for adults. If you are under 18, do not create an account.</li>\n<li><strong>Where we offer the Service.</strong> The Service is not offered in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or any country or region subject to comprehensive United States sanctions — currently Cuba, Iran, North Korea, and the Crimea, Donetsk and Luhansk regions of Ukraine. You confirm that you are not located in, or ordinarily resident in, any of those places, and that you are not a person with whom United States law prohibits us from dealing.</li>\n<li><strong>One person, one account.</strong> Give us accurate information, keep your password to yourself, and tell us at <a href=\"mailto:support@overhype.me\">support@overhype.me</a> if you think someone else is using your account. You are responsible for what happens under your account.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. What Overhype.me is</h2>\n<p>Overhype.me is a collection of deliberately exaggerated, humorous \"facts\" that anyone can personalise with a name, and a tool for turning a fact into a picture or meme. <strong>Everything on Overhype.me is comedy and hyperbole. No fact states anything true about any real person, including the person whose name is shown in it.</strong> Do not present a fact or a picture from Overhype.me as true.</p>\n<h2>3. Your content</h2>\n<p>\"Your content\" means anything you submit or create: facts, comments, the names you enter, photos you upload, and the memes and pictures you make.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You keep ownership</strong> of your content.</li>\n<li><strong>You give us a licence to run the Service with it</strong>: a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to host, store, copy, display, adapt (for example, to fit a meme layout), and distribute your content, and to let other people view and share content you make public, for as long as it is on the Service and for the periods described in our <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>. Facts you submit become part of the shared catalogue: when a fact is approved, the licence for that fact is perpetual and continues after you delete your account, and the fact is then credited to \"a former member\".</li>\n<li><strong>You are responsible for your content.</strong> You confirm that you have every right needed to post it and that it follows these Terms and our <a href=\"/guidelines\">Community Guidelines</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>We may review, refuse, edit for formatting, or remove</strong> any content, and we moderate submitted facts before they appear.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4. Photos and pictures of real people</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Only upload a photo of yourself.</strong> When you upload a photo you confirm that it shows you, that you are 18 or older, and that you have the right to use it. Do not upload a photo of anyone else, of a child, or of anyone who has not agreed.</li>\n<li><strong>What happens to a photo.</strong> To make a picture, your photo is sent to the image-generation services we use, as described in our <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>. Pictures are made by artificial intelligence.</li>\n<li><strong>Do not use the Service to depict anyone in a sexual, degrading, harassing or deceptive way</strong>, or to make a picture intended to be mistaken for a real photograph of a real event.</li>\n<li><strong>If a picture shows you without your permission</strong>, write to <a href=\"mailto:legal@overhype.me\">legal@overhype.me</a> with a link to it, and we will review it and remove it where appropriate. If it is an intimate or sexual image of you shared without your consent, say so in your message; we treat those requests first and remove valid ones within any time the law requires.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>\n<p>You agree not to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>break the law, or use the Service to help anyone else do so;</li>\n<li>post content that sexualises minors in any way — we report apparent child sexual abuse material to the National Center for Missing &#x26; Exploited Children as the law requires;</li>\n<li>post content that is hateful, threatens or harasses anyone, encourages violence or self-harm, or reveals someone's private information;</li>\n<li>impersonate anyone, choose a name intended to mislead people about who you are, or misrepresent your connection to any person or organisation;</li>\n<li>infringe anyone's copyright, trademark, privacy or publicity rights;</li>\n<li>send spam, use the share-by-email feature to contact people who do not want to hear from you, or manipulate votes or rankings;</li>\n<li>probe, scan or test the Service's security, get around any limit or safety control, use automated means to access or copy the Service, or interfere with its operation;</li>\n<li>use the Service from a place where it is not offered, or use technical means to hide where you are in order to do so.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The full list of what we allow is in our <a href=\"/guidelines\">Community Guidelines</a>.</p>\n<h2>6. Membership and payments</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Legendary membership</strong> is offered monthly or yearly, and payments are processed by Stripe. <strong>A monthly or yearly membership renews automatically</strong> at the end of each period, at the price shown when you joined unless we tell you of a change in advance, until you cancel.</li>\n<li><strong>You can cancel at any time</strong> from your profile. Your membership then stays active until the end of the period you have paid for and does not renew.</li>\n<li>If you think you were charged in error, write to <a href=\"mailto:support@overhype.me\">support@overhype.me</a>.</li>\n<li>Where we offer a one-time purchase, its terms are shown when you buy it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>7. Copyright complaints</h2>\n<p>We respond to notices of claimed copyright infringement as set out in our <a href=\"/copyright\">Copyright Policy</a>, and we end the accounts of people who repeatedly infringe.</p>\n<h2>8. Suspension and ending your account</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You can delete your account at any time</strong> from your profile. What we keep afterwards is described in our <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>We may suspend or end your account</strong>, or remove your content, if you break these Terms, if the law requires it, or to protect other people or the Service. Suspension stops you signing in; it does not by itself delete anything.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>9. The Service is provided \"as is\"</h2>\n<p>To the fullest extent the law allows, the Service is provided <strong>\"as is\" and \"as available\"</strong>, without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We do not promise that the Service will always be available, error-free or secure, or that pictures it makes will look any particular way.</p>\n<h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>\n<p>To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, data or goodwill, arising from your use of the Service. Our total liability for any claim relating to the Service is limited to the greater of the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim arose and US $50. Some places do not allow these limits, so they may not apply to you.</p>\n<h2>11. Indemnity</h2>\n<p>If someone brings a claim against us because of content you posted or your breach of these Terms, you agree to cover our reasonable costs and losses from that claim, to the extent the law allows.</p>\n<h2>12. Governing law and disputes</h2>\n<p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York and the federal laws of the United States, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute relating to these Terms or the Service will be heard only in the state or federal courts located in New York County, New York, and you and we consent to their jurisdiction.</p>\n<h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>\n<p>We may change these Terms. When we do, we will update the version at the top of this page and ask you to accept the new version before you continue using your account. If you do not accept it, you can delete your account.</p>\n<h2>14. Contact</h2>\n<p>Availeron Consulting, Inc., 745 5th Ave., Suite 500, New York, NY 10151, United States. Email: <a href=\"mailto:legal@overhype.me\">legal@overhype.me</a>.</p>";
